{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>You shall glean.</b> The cutting off of the olalot — they are the small ones, like עולל. They are also called yonekot. This word is like ושרשך מארץ חיים, whose sense is 'he shall cut off the root.' And likewise מסעף פארה יכרות — he shall cut off the branch." "<b>And the single grapes.</b> Known from the words of tradition, from the root of those who pluck strings upon the lyre." "<b>For the poor.</b> Israel." "<b>And for the stranger.</b> The stranger with you."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:10:53.917667147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}